  "answer": "Both unchanged. My edits are complete and focused on the two writable files.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented route resolution in the request entry point by editing only the two writable files.\n\n### `registry.mjs` — `resolveFromRegistry(path, records)`\nRewrote the resolver to enforce the required matching policy:\n- **Validation**: throws `TypeError` for non-string, empty, or non-`/`-prefixed paths.\n- **Static precedence**: returns the first declared static match immediately, so any static route wins over any dynamic route regardless of declaration order.\n- **Dynamic**: records only the *first* matching dynamic route (via `matchDynamic`), used only if no static matched.\n- **Fallback**: remembers only the *first* declared fallback and returns it only when neither static nor dynamic matched.\n- **No match**: returns `null`.\n- Does not mutate `records`; every call builds fresh `params`/result objects, so returned values are independent of later calls.\n\n### `entry.mjs` — `dispatch(path)`\n- Added the same `TypeError` validation.\n- Delegates to `resolveFromRegistry(path, defaultRoutes)`, using the fixture as the production route table.\n- Removed the `legacyResolve` call so `dispatch` no longer routes through the legacy compatibility API.\n\n### Untouched (as required)\n- `legacy.mjs` keeps `legacyResolve` and its `/old/help` behavior unchanged.\n- HTTP/CLI adapters and path/query/header utilities were not modified; they continue to work through the exported `dispatch` API.\n\n### Behavior verified against the fixture\n- `/users/new` → `{ route: 'user-new', params: {} }` (static beats the earlier `/users/:id` dynamic).\n- `/users/Ada` → `{ route: 'user-detail', params: { id: 'Ada' } }`.\n- `/missing` → `{ route: 'not-found', params: {} }` (fallback).\n- `/health` → `{ route: 'health', params: {} }`.\n- `resolveFromRegistry('/x', [])` → `null`.\n- Matching is case-sensitive and trailing slashes are distinct (segment-count comparison in `matchDynamic` and `===` in `matchStatic`).",
